{"tool_name":"scoary","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","debian","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"scoary","version":"1.6.16","home":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Microbial pan-GWAS using the output from Roary","identifiers":["biotools:Scoary","doi:10.1186/s13059-016-1108-8"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"entry_points":["scoary=scoary.methods:main","scoary_GUI=scoary.GUI:main"],"noarch":"python","number":2,"script":"python setup.py install --single-version-externally-managed --record=record.txt"},"requirements":{"host":["python","setuptools","scipy >=0.16","argparse","ete3","six"],"run":["python","scipy >=0.16","argparse","ete3","six"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary/archive/v1.6.16.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["scoary --help"],"imports":["scoary"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"scoary","identifiers":["biotools:Scoary","doi:10.1186/s13059-016-1108-8"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Pan-genome wide association studies and  is designed to take the gene_presence_absence.csv file from roary as well as a traits file created by the user and calculate the assocations between all genes in the accessory genome (all genes that are present in i genomes where 1 < i < n) and the traits. it reports a list of genes sorted by strength of association per trait.","home_url":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary","keywords":["Genotype and phenotype","Model organisms","GWAS study","Functional genomics","Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4796},"biotools":{"id":"scoary","home":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Pan-genome wide association studies and  is designed to take the gene_presence_absence.csv file from Roary as well as a traits file created by the user and calculate the assocations between all genes in the accessory genome (all genes that are present in i genomes where 1 < i < N) and the traits. It reports a list of genes sorted by strength of association per trait.","addition_date":"2016-09-12T15:20:53Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:18Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1.6.11"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scoary","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ola.brynildsrud@fhi.no","name":"Ola Brynildsrud","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla"},{"name":"Norwegian Institute of Public Health","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Ola Brynildsrud","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"UiO","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Vegard Eldholm","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary/blob/master/LICENSE"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Gene report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0916"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"note":"Scoary correlates the genes of an accessory genome to an observed phenotype (e.g. resistance towards a certain antibiotic compound, a particular pathotype etc.). It is thus a quick way of establishing possible genetic mechanisms of an expressed trait, not unlike a GWAS, but with the entire pan-genome rather than a core set of mutations. Scoary works on both bacteria, Archea and (in theory at least) viruses.","operation":[{"term":"Analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2945"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"P-value","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1669"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Scoary","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"UiO","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-016-1108-8","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author(s).Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have become indispensable in human medicine and genomics, but very few have been carried out on bacteria. Here we introduce Scoary, an ultra-fast, easy-to-use, and widely applicable software tool that scores the components of the pan-genome for associations to observed phenotypic traits while accounting for population stratification, with minimal assumptions about evolutionary processes. We call our approach pan-GWAS to distinguish it from traditional, single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)-based GWAS. Scoary is implemented in Python and is available under an open source GPLv3 license at https://github.com/AdmiralenOla/Scoary.","authors":[{"name":"Bohlin J."},{"name":"Brynildsrud O."},{"name":"Eldholm V."},{"name":"Scheffer L."}],"citationCount":154,"date":"2016-11-25T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Rapid scoring of genes in microbial pan-genome-wide association studies with Scoary"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Functional genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0085"},{"term":"GWAS study","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3517"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Scoary","home":"https://bio.tools/scoary","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"1.6.11","summary":"Pan-genome wide association studies and  is designed to take the gene_presence_absence.csv file from Roary as well as a traits file created by the user and calculate the assocations between all genes in the accessory genome (all genes that are present in i genomes where 1 < i < N) and the traits. It reports a list of genes sorted by strength of association per trait.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@TOOL_VERSION@","first_commit":"2021-03-18","conda_name":"scoary","conda_version":"1.6.16","summary":"Scoary calculates the assocations between all genes in the accessory genome and the traits.","edam_operations":["Ana